  "description": "SAHSED crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H56 N12 O16 Tb4,3(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.811-3.949 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.79-115.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C75H69N12O20Tb4.",
